# Lab 3b-2: System Services & Network Shares Setup

## Overview
This lab covers the configuration and status verification of essential Linux system services, network file sharing (Samba & NFS), containerization (Docker), and database services.

## Services Configured and Verified
- **Samba (SMB)**: Created `[LabShare]` mapped to `/srv/samba/share` with guest access. Verified via `testparm -s` and `systemctl status smbd`.
- **NFS**: Exported `/var/nfs/lab_share`. Verified using `showmount -e localhost` and `systemctl status nfs-kernel-server`.
- **MariaDB**: Active and running (`systemctl status mariadb`).
- **Docker**: Active daemon (`systemctl status docker`) and successfully verified container execution using `docker run hello-world`.
- **Chrony & Rsyslog**: Time synchronization and system logging services verified active.

